{"id":"rule-churn-by-code","title":"Which codes are amended most","question":"Which of the City's codes do these ordinances amend?","finding":"The Planning Code is amended most often: 337 ordinances in 9 years (56 adding a requirement or fee, 95 removing, waiving or exempting), followed by the Administrative Code (120) and the Police Code (65). The Building Code was amended by 54 and the Public Works Code by 55.","how":"The code is read from the start of each ordinance's short title (\"Planning Code - ...\"). An ordinance naming two codes is counted under each, so the rows add to more than the number of ordinances.","limits":"Many Planning Code ordinances are landmark designations or changes for a single district rather than citywide rules. Ordinances whose short title names no code (appropriations, agreements, uncodified fee waivers) are grouped in one row.","tier":"REDFLAG","columns":[{"k":"code","t":"Code named in the title","type":"text"},{"k":"all","t":"Ordinances","type":"int"},{"k":"adds","t":"Add a requirement or fee","type":"int"},{"k":"cuts","t":"Remove a step, waive or exempt","type":"int"},{"k":"both","t":"Do both","type":"int"},{"k":"feeUp","t":"Raises or creates a fee","type":"int"},{"k":"feeDown","t":"Waives, cuts or defers a fee","type":"int"},{"k":"streamline","t":"Streamlines or removes a step","type":"int"},{"k":"exempt","t":"Exempts or makes an exception","type":"int"},{"k":"require","t":"Adds a requirement, permit or restriction","type":"int"},{"k":"landmark","t":"Designates a landmark","type":"int"},{"k":"map","t":"Changes a zoning map or special district","type":"int"},{"k":"money","t":"Budget, bond, lawsuit or agreement (not sorted)","type":"int"},{"k":"neither","t":"None of these words","type":"int"}],"rows":[{"code":"Planning Code","all":337,"adds":56,"cuts":95,"both":23,"neither":73,"money":1,"feeUp":3,"feeDown":24,"streamline":60,"exempt":38,"require":53,"landmark":82,"map":84},{"code":"No code named in the short title","all":261,"adds":1